  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Industrialist Vinod Sekhar brought Green Rubber into a partnership with Timberland to put recycled tyre material into footwear. The planned shoe outsoles combined reclaimed rubber with new material, aiming to preserve durability while reducing reliance on virgin rubber. For Sekhar, finding recognisable consumer products was part of making the recycling process commercially useful.\n\nHis collection of Mickey Mouse ties reflects another business interest: Walt Disney’s ability to make entertainment profitable. He wore one to an early meeting with bankers despite advisers warning that it would undermine his credibility. The ties became a regular part of his wardrobe, expressing his admiration for a company built around making people happy.",
    "html": "<p>Industrialist Vinod Sekhar brought Green Rubber into a partnership with Timberland to put recycled tyre material into footwear. The planned shoe outsoles combined reclaimed rubber with new material, aiming to preserve durability while reducing reliance on virgin rubber. For Sekhar, finding recognisable consumer products was part of making the recycling process commercially useful.</p>\r\n<p>His collection of Mickey Mouse ties reflects another business interest: Walt Disney’s ability to make entertainment profitable. He wore one to an early meeting with bankers despite advisers warning that it would undermine his credibility. The ties became a regular part of his wardrobe, expressing his admiration for a company built around making people happy.</p>\r\n",
